@baseUrl = http://localhost:5205

### ================================================================
### 1. POST /api/registrations
### ================================================================

### Case 01 - Valid Competitor, partly paid -> 201, CS27-0026, fee 2500, Pending, Partial
# @name case01
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1001",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 02 - Valid Exhibitor, not paid -> 201, fee 1500, Unpaid, Pending
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1002",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 0
}

### Case 03 - Valid VIP, fully paid -> 201, fee 5000, Paid
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1003",
  "registrationType": "VIP",
  "amountPaid": 5000
}

### Case 04 - Numbers increase: compare the 3 responses above (CS27-0026, 0027, 0028)

### Case 05 - Client sends server-only fields -> 201, extras ignored (fee 5000, Pending, next CS27 number)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1005",
  "registrationType": "VIP",
  "amountPaid": 0,
  "registrationFee": 1,
  "status": "Confirmed",
  "registrationNumber": "HACK-1"
}

### Case 06 - All text fields empty -> 400, errors for all six fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "",
  "contactNumber": "",
  "email": "",
  "address": "",
  "carMakeModel": "",
  "plateNumber": "",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 07 - Invalid contact number -> 400, errors.ContactNumber
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "12345",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1007",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 08 - Invalid email -> 400, errors.Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan-at-example",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1008",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 09 - Paid more than the fee -> 400, errors.AmountPaid (cannot exceed 1,500)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1009",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 2000
}

### Case 10 - Negative amount paid -> 400, errors.AmountPaid (must be 0 or more)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1010",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": -100
}

### Case 11 - Unknown registration type -> 400, nothing created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1011",
  "registrationType": "Sponsor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 12 - participantName of 151 characters -> 400, errors.ParticipantName (150 limit)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789X",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1012",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### Case 13 - Duplicate plate (same as Case 01) -> 409, title Registration.Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1001",
  "registrationType": "Competitor",
  "amountPaid": 1000.00
}

### ================================================================
### 2. GET /api/registrations (paging)
### ================================================================

### Case 14 - Default list -> 200, page 1, pageSize 10, totalCount >= 25
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations

### Case 15 - Newest first: same request, check order (TC-01..05 at the top)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations

### Case 16 - Second page, custom size -> page 2, pageSize 5, 5 items
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=2&pageSize=5

### Case 17 - Page past the end -> 200, items [], totalCount unchanged
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=999

### Case 18 - Invalid page -> 400, errors.Page
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?page=0

### Case 19 - Page size too large -> 400, errors.PageSize (1-50)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?pageSize=100

### ================================================================
### 3. GET /api/registrations (filters)
### ================================================================

### Case 20 - By type -> every item VIP, includes Case 03
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?type=VIP

### Case 21 - By status -> every item Confirmed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?status=Confirmed

### Case 22 - By participant name -> every name contains "juan", includes Case 01
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=juan

### Case 23 - Name search ignores case -> same items and totalCount as Case 22
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=JUAN

### Case 24 - Partial name match -> includes "Juan Dela Cruz"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=dela

### Case 25 - Combined filters -> every item matches all three, includes Case 01
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?type=Competitor&status=Pending&participantName=juan

### Case 26 - No matches -> items [], totalCount 0, totalPages 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?participantName=zzzzzz

### Case 27 - Invalid type -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?type=Sponsor

### Case 28 - Invalid status -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations?status=Done

### ================================================================
### 4. GET /api/registrations/{id}
### ================================================================

### Case 29 - Existing ID (taken from Case 01) -> 200, same data as Case 01
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/{{case01.response.body.$.id}}

### Case 30 - ID that doesn't exist -> 404, title Registration.NotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Case 31 - Not a valid GUID -> 404, no 500
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/abc

### ================================================================
### 5. GET /api/registrations/summary
### ================================================================

### Case 32 - Summary returns all 8 fields (also Cases 33, 34, 35, 36, 38 use this response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary

### Case 37 - Summary updates after a new registration
### Step 1: run the summary above and note the numbers
### Step 2: run this POST
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantName": "Juan Dela Cruz",
  "contactNumber": "09171234567",
  "email": "juan.delacruz@example.com",
  "address": "123 Rizal St., Naga City",
  "carMakeModel": "Toyota Supra MK4",
  "plateNumber": "TST 1037",
  "registrationType": "Exhibitor",
  "amountPaid": 500
}

### Step 3: summary again -> total +1, pending +1, fees +1500, payments +500, uncollected +1000
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary

### Case 38 - /summary is not treated as an ID -> 200 summary, not 404/400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/summary